Input: {"question": "In which significant event was Bioprinting process involved?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 73, "text": "**Bioprinting Process and Its Involvement in a Significant Event Filing**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 75, "end": 242, "text": "The bioprinting process, a revolutionary technology in the field of biotechnology, has been involved in a significant event filing, as evidenced by US patent 11517453."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 243, "end": 401, "text": "This article provides an overview of the bioprinting process and its role in the filing, highlighting the legal and technological aspects of this development."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 402, "end": 425, "text": "**Bioprinting Process**"}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 427, "end": 517, "text": "Bioprinting is a 3D printing technique used to create functional living tissue and organs."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 518, "end": 662, "text": "It involves the layer-by-layer deposition of biomaterials, such as cells, proteins, and biomolecules, to create complex structures and patterns."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 663, "end": 851, "text": "The bioprinting process has the potential to transform the field of medicine, enabling the creation of artificial organs for transplantation, tissue engineering, and regenerative medicine."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 852, "end": 874, "text": "**US Patent 11517453**"}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 876, "end": 1033, "text": "On January 11, 2022, the United States Patent and Trademark Office (USPTO) granted patent 11517453, titled \"Bioprinting of Organ-Specific Tissue Constructs.\""}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1034, "end": 1232, "text": "This patent describes a bioprinting process for creating organ-specific tissue constructs, which can be used for various medical applications, including tissue engineering and regenerative medicine."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1233, "end": 1278, "text": "**Involvement in a Significant Event Filing**"}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1280, "end": 1422, "text": "The bioprinting process was involved in a significant event filing, as evidenced by the legal filing claim associated with US patent 11517453."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1423, "end": 1578, "text": "This filing marks a significant milestone in the development of bioprinting technology, demonstrating its potential to revolutionize the field of medicine."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1579, "end": 1619, "text": "**Legal and Technological Implications**"}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1621, "end": 1747, "text": "The involvement of the bioprinting process in a significant event filing has significant legal and technological implications."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1748, "end": 1909, "text": "From a legal perspective, the patent filing and grant demonstrate the recognition of bioprinting as a valuable technology with potential commercial applications."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1910, "end": 2123, "text": "From a technological perspective, the bioprinting process has the potential to transform the field of medicine, enabling the creation of artificial organs and tissues for transplantation and regenerative medicine."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2124, "end": 2138, "text": "**References**"}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2140, "end": 2184, "text": "* United States Patent and Trademark Office."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2185, "end": 2192, "text": "(2022)."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2193, "end": 2258, "text": "Patent 11517453: Bioprinting of Organ-Specific Tissue Constructs."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2259, "end": 2321, "text": "Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/patents.uspto.gov\\/patent\\/11517453>"}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2322, "end": 2334, "text": "* Murphy, S."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2335, "end": 2350, "text": "V., & Atala, A."}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2351, "end": 2358, "text": "(2014)."}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2359, "end": 2396, "text": "3D bioprinting of tissues and organs."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 65, "text": "**Bioprinting Process and Royal Assent: A Historical Connection**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 67, "end": 235, "text": "The bioprinting process, a revolutionary technology in the field of regenerative medicine, has a lesser-known connection to the centuries-old tradition of royal assent."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 236, "end": 377, "text": "While seemingly unrelated, these two concepts intersected in a significant event that marked a turning point in the history of biotechnology."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 378, "end": 392, "text": "**Background**"}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 394, "end": 528, "text": "Bioprinting, as described in US patent 11517453, is a process that utilizes 3D printing technology to create functional living tissue."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 529, "end": 633, "text": "This innovative method has far-reaching implications for the treatment of various diseases and injuries."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 634, "end": 793, "text": "On the other hand, royal assent is a formal approval of a proposed law in monarchies, where the sovereign's consent is required for legislation to take effect."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 794, "end": 836, "text": "**The Event: The Bioprinting Act of 2015**"}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 838, "end": 1006, "text": "In 2015, the United Kingdom's Parliament passed the Bioprinting Act, a landmark legislation aimed at regulating and promoting the development of bioprinting technology."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1007, "end": 1148, "text": "The Act, which received widespread support from both the scientific community and lawmakers, was sent to Queen Elizabeth II for royal assent."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1149, "end": 1290, "text": "On February 12, 2015, the Queen granted royal assent to the Bioprinting Act, marking a significant milestone in the history of biotechnology."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1291, "end": 1461, "text": "This event not only underscored the UK's commitment to advancing medical research but also highlighted the potential of bioprinting to transform the healthcare landscape."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1462, "end": 1488, "text": "**Studies and References**"}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1490, "end": 1599, "text": "Several studies have examined the impact of the Bioprinting Act on the development of bioprinting technology."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1600, "end": 1796, "text": "A 2017 study published in the journal _Regenerative Medicine_ found that the Act led to a significant increase in bioprinting research funding and collaborations between academia and industry (1)."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1797, "end": 1979, "text": "Another study published in _Nature Biotechnology_ in 2019 noted that the Act's regulatory framework facilitated the establishment of bioprinting startups and spin-offs in the UK (2)."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1980, "end": 2089, "text": "In addition, historians have analyzed the significance of royal assent in the context of the Bioprinting Act."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2090, "end": 2305, "text": "A 2020 article in the _Journal of Modern History_ argued that the Queen's approval of the Act symbolized the monarchy's adaptability to emerging technologies and its commitment to supporting scientific progress (3)."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2306, "end": 2320, "text": "**Conclusion**"}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2322, "end": 2486, "text": "The connection between the bioprinting process and royal assent may seem unexpected, but it highlights the complex interplay between science, politics, and history."}}, "original_cards": [], "current_answers": ["Granting of US Patent 11517453", "Royal assent to the Bioprinting Act of 2015"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Granting of US Patent 11517453", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Royal assent to the Bioprinting Act of 2015", "origin": "initial"}]}
